diff --git a/docs/source/whats_new.rst b/docs/source/whats_new.rst
index 9c7935aee7..b3424ea1b2 100644
--- a/docs/source/whats_new.rst
+++ b/docs/source/whats_new.rst
@@ -97,6 +97,7 @@ Requirements
 
 Bugs
 ~~~~
+- Render motor-execution datasets (:class:`moabb.datasets.Thapa2025`, :class:`moabb.datasets.Kueper2024`, :class:`moabb.datasets.NeBULA2025`, :class:`moabb.datasets.PerezBlanco2026`, :class:`moabb.datasets.Schirrmeister2017`, :class:`moabb.datasets.GuttmannFlury2025_ME`, and :class:`moabb.datasets.Wu2020`) as **Motor Execution** instead of **Motor Imagery** in the automated Stimulus Protocol timeline diagram, dataset webpage header, and metadata catalog (reported by Bhoj Raj Thapa, fixed by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Fix :class:`moabb.datasets.Kueper2024` keeping error trials (rest shorter than 5 s, marker ``S3``) and additional trials (``S27``) as movement events: only onsets followed by the end-of-correct-trial marker ``S128`` are kept, 40 per recording set. Also download the subjects a partial cache lacks instead of returning no runs: ``data_path`` checked only that the dataset folder existed, so a cache from version 1 or from the NEMAR deposit (subjects 1-8) would have loaded subjects 9-14 empty (:gh:`1333` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Fix :class:`moabb.datasets.Cho2017` giving the pre-cue segment a class-dependent offset. The GigaDB files store each class as a stream of tiled 7-s trial blocks (2 s fixation, then the cue), and the loader removed the mean of each class stream as a whole; since some participants make a sustained eye movement toward the imagined hand after the cue, that mean differs by class, so without a high-pass filter (``fmin=None``) the pre-cue segment of every trial carried an offset of about half the post-cue step, with the opposite sign. The loader now removes from each block the mean of its own fixation period (subject 5, F8-F7 in the second before the cue, right minus left: -4313 before, +7 after, in file units). The default 8-32 Hz band and the default 0-3 s interval give identical data. A high-pass of 0.1-1 Hz removes the mean of the tiled block pattern itself and puts the offset back whatever the loader does; the docstring now documents the data layout and recommends the default ``fmin`` or a pre-cue ``baseline`` in that case. Adds an offline regression test on a synthetic tiled file (:gh:`1340` by `Yiheng Li`_).
 - Fix :func:`moabb.analysis.plotting.summary_plot` raising ``ValueError: The truth value of a Series is ambiguous`` when two pipeline names shorten to the same first word, such as ``Tangent Space LR`` and ``Tangent Space SVM Grid`` from ``pipelines/``. It now keeps the full names and logs a warning, the same as ``analyze`` already does (by `Iain`_).
